<title>FINLAND: FINNISH FEB CORE INFLATION +/-0 PCT YR/YR.</title>
<headline>FINNISH FEB CORE INFLATION +/-0 PCT YR/YR.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish core inflation was</p>
<p>+/-0 percent year-on-year in February and it rose 0.2 percent</p>
<p>month-on-month, Statistics Finland said in a statement on</p>
<p>Tuesday.</p>
<p>The mean of four economists' forecasts for the February</p>
<p>core inflation rate had been for a 0.2 percent rise in a +/-0</p>
<p>percent to +0.3 percent range.</p>
<p>The Bank of Finland's target for the year-on-year change in</p>
<p>the underlying rate of inflation -- its chief gauge for</p>
<p>monetary policy -- is a rise of no more than around two</p>
<p>percent.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
